* (-) 42. [APP] ACME App

  Internal team workspace for asynchronous collaboration. Combines
  real-time messaging, shared notes, and activity dashboards into a
  single platform accessible via web and mobile.

  Tech stack:
  - Backend: Python / FastAPI / PostgreSQL / Redis
  - Frontend: TypeScript / React / Next.js
  - Mobile: TypeScript / React Native (iOS + Android)
  - Infrastructure: Terraform / AWS (ECS, RDS, ElastiCache, S3, SQS, CloudFront)
  - CI/CD: GitHub Actions

  Lifecycle per feature stage:
  ~ *Design* — Architecture, user stories, data models, flow diagrams
  ~ *Implementation* — Source code split by platform: Backend, Frontend, Mobile
  ~ *Verification* — Unit tests, integration tests, E2E tests
  ~ *Validation* — QA scenarios, acceptance scripts, sign-off

  /`[infra]` and `[ops]` elements use flat structures verified by CI
  tooling, not the four-phase lifecycle./

  /Individual defects are tracked in the issue tracker; the SDWBS records
  aggregated counts in the Implementation phase./

  Release stages define project-wide milestones. Feature-level stages are
  independent work packages within each module — they may use scope-based
  increments (e.g. "Direct Messaging" → "Group Chat") or fidelity-based
  progression (e.g. "Wireframe" → "Functional" → "Polished"). Feature
  stages do not need to align 1:1 with release stages.

  - `Stage 1` — MVP: auth, direct messaging, notes, push notifications, core infra
  - `Stage 2` — Growth: OAuth/2FA, group chat, email digests, CDN, monitoring
  - /Future/ — Dashboard analytics, collaborative editing, advanced reporting

  /Stages are not strict gates — modules may complete stage work independently./

  /See `README.norg` for full SDWBS conventions./


