** (-) 42.6. [infra] Cloud Infrastructure {* 42.6}

   Infrastructure-as-code modules. Each is an atomic component verified
   by `terraform validate` in CI.

   Environments: `dev` | `staging` | `prod`

*** (x) 42.6.1. `network` — VPC & DNS {* 42.6.1}
    Three-tier network: public (ALB, NAT, CloudFront), private (compute),
    database (isolated). DNS records for API and web domains.

*** (x) 42.6.2. `compute` — Container Cluster & Services {* 42.6.2}
    ECS Fargate cluster with API, worker, and web server task definitions.
    Pre-requisites:
    - (x) {* 42.6.1} Network
    - (x) {* 42.6.7} Secrets — container environment variables
    - (x) {* 42.6.9} Container Registry

*** (x) 42.6.3. `database` — PostgreSQL {* 42.6.3}
    RDS PostgreSQL with read replica for analytics queries.
    Pre-requisites:
    - (x) {* 42.6.1} Network — database subnet group

*** (x) 42.6.4. `cache` — Redis {* 42.6.4}
    ElastiCache Redis for session store, rate limiting counters, and
    real-time presence (chat online status).
    Pre-requisites:
    - (x) {* 42.6.1} Network

*** (x) 42.6.5. `storage` — Object Storage {* 42.6.5}
    S3 buckets for user uploads (avatars, chat attachments, note images)
    and static asset hosting.

*** (x) 42.6.6. `queue` — Message Queue {* 42.6.6}
    SQS queues for async notification dispatch and chat message fan-out.
    Dead-letter queues with alarm integration.

*** (x) 42.6.7. `secrets` — Secrets Manager {* 42.6.7}
    Database credentials, OAuth client secrets, push provider keys,
    API signing keys.

*** (-) 42.6.8. `cdn` — Content Delivery Network {* 42.6.8}
    CloudFront distribution for static assets and media attachments.
    Pre-requisites:
    - (x) {* 42.6.5} Storage — origin bucket
    - (x) {* 42.6.1} Network — DNS alias records

    - (x) Terraform module: distribution, origin, cache policy
    - (x) DNS alias records for assets subdomain
    - (-) Cache invalidation automation on deploy
    - ( ) Signed URL generation for private content

*** (-) 42.6.9. `registry` — Container Registry {* 42.6.9}
    ECR repositories for API, worker, and web server images.

*** (-) 42.6.10. Monitoring & Alerting {* 42.6.10}

    Pre-requisites:
    - (x) {* 42.6.2} Compute — log groups
    - (x) {* 42.6.6} Queue — dead-letter queue metrics

    Alarms (per environment):
    - API: 5xx rate, 4xx surge, P95/P99 latency, CPU/memory utilisation
    - Worker: crash patterns, failed invocations, missed schedules
    - Queue: DLQ depth, oldest message age
    - Database: connection count, replication lag, storage threshold


